* The jump pads in the seas throw creatures out onto a shore (openc2e
* Creatures 2 project, our own script). Run by openc2e after the world loads
* (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
*
* Owner, 2026-11-18 (picture sea-launcher-east.png): of the options for the
* sea jump pads, "arc to a shore". The game has three jump pads (2 13 1) in
* the seas set to launch: the east seabed (6820, 1048; mode 1, velocity
* -250, -900), the west seabed (461, 1254; mode 2, +270, -1200) and the
* west sea (830, 938; mode 1). openc2e moved a launched creature by that
* velocity in a single tick, to the top of the world, and it fell straight
* back into the sea where it started (one norn was flung 11 times in 8
* minutes). A patch to the pad's own script (script-patches.txt) now hands
* each creature it launches (modes 1 and 2) to a carrier (2 1 163) instead,
* which throws it in an arc onto the nearest dry shore the pad points at:
*   east seabed pad, thrown west: the dock planks above the east sea's
*     west end (middle x 6440, feet 654; room 13, over the sealed water
*     under the dock: west of x 6320 the planks are open to the cave below)
*   west seabed pad, thrown east: the sand at the west sea's east shore
*     (middle x 1090, feet 628; room 3)
*   west sea pad, thrown west: the beach at the west sea's west shore
*     (middle x 140, feet 633; room 128)
* The arc takes 28 ticks: straight from where the creature stood to where it
* lands, lifted by a parabola (its height h in the middle, enough to clear
* the rocks between). Moved by script (MVTO with WAIT 1), so it is no fall
* to learn from or be hurt by. OV95 marks a creature in the air (the pads,
* the airlock, the shelf current and the submarine leave it alone). A pad
* that has been carried out of the water throws as the game's script did.
* The pads on land (mode 0) and mode 3 are unchanged.
enum 2 1 163 kill targ next
scrp 2 1 163 9
  tick 0
  inst
* var0, var1 where the creature starts (its left edge and top); var2, var3
* where it lands (likewise); var4 the arc's height; var5 the step (0-28)
  targ ov01
  setv var0 posl
  setv var9 rtyp
  targ ownr
  doif var9 ne 2
*   (a pad out of the water: the game's own throw)
    setv var2 ov02
    setv var3 ov03
    targ ov00
    setv velx var2
    setv vely var3
    setv ov95 0
    targ ownr
    kill ownr
    stop
  endi
  doif var0 gt 5000
    setv var2 6440
    setv var3 654
    setv var4 250
  else
    doif var0 lt 640
      setv var2 1090
      setv var3 628
      setv var4 300
    else
      setv var2 140
      setv var3 633
      setv var4 250
    endi
  endi
  targ ov00
  setv var0 posl
  setv var1 post
  setv var9 posr
  subv var9 posl
  divv var9 2
  subv var2 var9
  setv var9 posb
  subv var9 post
  subv var3 var9
  setv var5 0
  loop
    addv var5 1
*   across: var0 + (var2 - var0) * step / 28
    setv var8 var2
    subv var8 var0
    mulv var8 var5
    divv var8 28
    addv var8 var0
*   and up: var1 + (var3 - var1) * step / 28 - 4 h step (28 - step) / 784
    setv var9 28
    subv var9 var5
    mulv var9 var5
    mulv var9 var4
    divv var9 196
    setv var7 var3
    subv var7 var1
    mulv var7 var5
    divv var7 28
    addv var7 var1
    subv var7 var9
    mvto var8 var7
    setv velx 0
    setv vely 0
    wait 1
    inst
  untl var5 ge 28
  setv vely 1
  setv ov95 0
  targ ownr
  kill ownr
endm
* (after a load, no carriers are left and no creature is in the air)
enum 4 0 0 setv ov95 0 next
